WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.009
Well, here's a surprise: James Gunn's The
Suicide Squad might just feature a Big Bad

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:08.530
who is... well, pretty big and pretty bad.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.660
Rumor-slinging website We Got This Covered
is reporting that their oh-so anonymous sources

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.990
tell them that the main villain of the upcoming
soft reboot will be none other than Vandal

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.820
Savage, an iconic DC villain with a very long
history.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.710
The gang being assembled for The Suicide Squad
is an interesting mix of the familiar and

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.710
the new.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.009
Margot Robbie will be reprising her role as
Harley Quinn, arguably the star of the show

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:34.809
the first time around; also returning are
Viola Davis as Amanda Waller, Joel Kinnaman

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:38.829
as team leader Rick Flag, and Jai Courtney
as Captain Boomerang.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:43.230
New to the proceedings this time around are
David Dastmalchian as Polka-Dot Man, Daniela

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.679
Melchior as a gender-flipped version of the
criminal known as Ratcatcher, and Steve Agee

00:00:47.679 --> 00:00:49.600
as the voice of King Shark.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.160
A slew of famous names have also been cast
in undisclosed roles, although John Cena is

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.750
widely believed to be taking on the role of
Peacemaker, a vigilante so stridently committed

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.379
to the cause of peace that he'll straight-up
kill you if you aren't.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:06.939
Also among the cast are Idris Elba, Storm
Reid, Nathan Fillion, Michael Rooker, Peter

00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:09.220
Capaldi, and Taika Waititi.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.090
Plot rumors suggest that the movie will see
Waller sending in the Suicide Squad to deal

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:17.200
with some kind of alien beast that has been
held captive in a secret prison built by the

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.680
Nazis during the Second World War.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.660
This monster is now under the sway of two
villains, referred to in the synopsis only

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.799
as "the Mayor" and "the General."

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:30.062
These rather official-sounding names may indeed
hint at Savage, as in the pages of DC comics,

00:01:30.062 --> 00:01:34.350
the villain has played a part in world events
throughout all of history.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:39.719
Savage came into the world as an actual caveman,
but was granted a powerful intellect and immortality

00:01:39.719 --> 00:01:44.440
by a mysterious, radioactive meteorite that
fell to Earth in his vicinity.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.880
He's basically been playing the governments
and societies of the world like a fiddle for

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.620
roughly 50,000 years, and it's suggested that
he may have taken on the mantle of a wide

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.329
array of different historical figures.

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:59.570
Oh, and he's been revered as a god and exalted
as a ruler by multiple civilizations throughout

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:00.570
history.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.450
So yeah, how's that for a Big Bad?

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:08.140
Obviously, it needs to be said that this rumor
should be taken with about six pounds of salt.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.330
We Got This Covered is hardly the most reliable
source of inside info, and while the site

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:16.650
has fielded accurate rumor reports in the
past, it has also fielded more than its fair

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.620
of share of complete bunk.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.709
It should also be pointed out that the plot
synopsis has in no way been confirmed, and

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:26.190
that Gunn himself has said that a good deal
of the rumors floating about concerning The

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.690
Suicide Squad are untrue.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:31.959
There have also been a good number of other
baddies rumored for the film.

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:36.069
Other "inside sources" have asserted, for
example, that Capaldi will be portraying frequent

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:40.690
Teen Titans antagonist Psimon, while some
have insisted that the alien monster mentioned

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:45.420
in the synopsis will be none other than J'Onn
J'Onnz, also known as Martian Manhunter.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.680
Until Gunn decides to give fans some inside
info or even a trailer all of this should

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.650
be taken as pure speculation.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.010
The truth is, nobody outside of the production
yet knows who The Suicide Squad's main antagonist

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.010
will be.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.860
Well, almost nobody, that is.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:03.349
Speaking on his Fatman Beyond podcast last
June, filmmaker and quintessential comic book

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:08.070
geek Kevin Smith revealed that he is, in fact,
privy to that particular information.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:11.480
Smith asked his audience if they had heard
the news about the movie's villain, and when

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.350
nobody responded in the affirmative, he admitted
he had figured everyone knew already.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:18.519
"I thought that everybody knew and I was about
to say but I was like Wait…

00:03:18.519 --> 00:03:19.560
I might have heard that.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.160
“Feel free to break something.”

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.810
“I might have heard that privately."

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:26.689
Unfortunately, Smith was reluctant to spill
any details about what he'd heard — but

00:03:26.689 --> 00:03:28.830
what he did say was pretty encouraging.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:33.209
"If it is what I heard it is f------ phenomenal.

00:03:33.209 --> 00:03:35.470
And boy it is in the right hands with James
Gunn"

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:38.200
Well, then: bring on August 2021.

